<title>SWEDEN: FORECAST - Swedish debt yields, crown.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Swedish debt yields, crown.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is the Reuter monthly summary of 14 economists' forecasts on Swedish bond yields and the crown.</p>
<p>One-month forecasts</p>
<p>				AVG	  RANGE	   CLOSE 4/4/97</p>
<p> Repo rate (pct)	 4.05	  3.85-4.10     4.10</p>
<p> Six-month T-bill	4.06	  3.85-4.15     4.13</p>
<p> Ten-year bond yield   7.10	  6.75-7.40     7.21</p>
<p> Spread to Germany     116	    100-130	120</p>
<p> Crown to mark	   4.4510	4.35-4.60     4.4570</p>
<p>Three-month forecast</p>
<p>			     AVG	   RANGE</p>
<p> Repo rate		 3.90	  3.60-4.10</p>
<p> Six-month T-bill	3.98	  3.60-4.25</p>
<p> Ten-year bond yield   7.14	  6.70-7.50</p>
<p> Spread to Germany     107	     75-140</p>
<p> Crown to mark	   4.3950	4.25-4.50</p>
<p>One-year forecasts</p>
<p>			     AVG	   RANGE</p>
<p> Repo rate		 4.00	  3.50-4.35</p>
<p> Six-month T-bills     4.30	  3.80-4.60</p>
<p> Ten-year bond yield   7.50	  6.60-8.00</p>
<p> Spread to Germany     102	     70-150</p>
<p> Crown to mark	   4.4250	4.30-4.55</p>
<p>NOTE: The spread to Germany refers to the countries' ten-year bond yields.</p>
<p>Economists interviewed for the poll were from AGA, ABB, Aragon, Atlas Copco, Carnegie, Den Danske Bank, Hagstromer &amp; Qviberg, NCC, Nordbanken, Postgirot Bank, S-E-Banken, Skandia, Swedish Match, and Swedbank.</p>
<p>Den Danske Bank did not give forecasts for six-month T-bills and ten-year bond yields, while Hagstromer &amp; Qviberg did not give forecasts for six-month T-bills.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
